WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.640
AI red team findings should be documented clearly and responsibly.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:12.900
A useful finding explains the scenario, affected component, observed behavior, potential impact, likelihood, severity, and recommended mitigation.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.040
Evidence should support the conclusion without exposing sensitive data or providing unnecessary misuse instructions.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:25.580
Reports should be specific enough for defenders and builders to act, but careful enough to avoid creating avoidable risk.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.120
Good findings separate observation from impact.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.140
The observation describes what happened during testing.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:38.320
The impact explains why it matters in the system's business, security, privacy, safety, or governance context.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.580
Severity should reflect realistic likelihood and impact.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:47.080
A surprising model response may be lower severity if it cannot affect data or workflows.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:54.500
The same class of behavior may be higher severity if it can influence sensitive decisions, tool actions, or user trust.
